    "result_text": "The full test suite passes (`BUILD SUCCESS`, 1 test run, 0 failures).\n\n## Summary\n\nImplemented the rule so that creating an owner whose lower-cased email is already used by any other owner is rejected with **409 Conflict**, following the existing duplicate-telephone pattern:\n\n1. **`DuplicateEmailException`** (new) \u2014 a `RuntimeException` mirroring `DuplicateTelephoneException`.\n\n2. **`ExceptionControllerAdvice`** \u2014 added a `@ExceptionHandler` for `DuplicateEmailException` that renders a `409 Conflict` `ProblemDetail`, plus the `ERROR_DUPLICATE_EMAIL` message constant.\n\n3. **`OwnerRestControllerV1`** \u2014 added a `rejectDuplicateEmail(...)` call to `prepareNewOwner` (right after email normalization/telephone check) and the method itself. It reuses the existing `canonicalEmail(...)` (trim + lower-case) as the single definition of email identity, treats a `null`/omitted email as never-duplicate, and throws when any existing owner's canonicalized email matches.\n\nThe acceptance test `coreRejectsDuplicateEmail` \u2014 which creates an owner with an email then expects a second create with the same email to return 409 \u2014 passes.",
